assert `jg_m1' == 1 & `jg_m2' == 1
// The axis and side titles are declared as title() is, string asis, so the
// quotes the user typed reach the spec.  Declared string, Stata stripped
// them: ytitle("line 1" "line 2") was stored, and drawn, as one line, and
// xtitle(`"a "b" c"') as a "b" c, its own quotes gone (measured 24sep2026).
// twoway's SVG export, measured the same day, draws the first as two
// lines, "line 1" and "line 2", the second as a "b" c, and each '90s
// title below as '90s x, '90s y ...; it refuses the plain xtitle("'90s x")
// and t1title("'90s t1"), r(109).  The page is held to what this tree's
// renderer draws as twoway does; a "b" c is the renderer's own text
// reader's to draw (test_textbox_multiline.py) and is held here to what is
// stored.  t1title() .. r2title() are stored and named, not drawn.
capture dash clear
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, ytitle("line 1" "line 2") xtitle(`"a "b" c"') name(jg46i)
local jg_t1 = _rc
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, xtitle("'90s x") ytitle(`"'90s y"') t1title("'90s t1") b2title(`"'90s b2"') name(jg46j)
local jg_t2 = _rc
